[17592186484245 #edb/ref 1069 "q-91200" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484245 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484245 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}9 & 3 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{12}$ equal to zero.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484245 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "858b58f0-f246-57e1-b5d7-2b4a24d86dda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484245 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{12}=3$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}9 & 3 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-3){C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-2){C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -2 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -2 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484254 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484254 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42570" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484254 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592